          "verdict": "Fixes CVE-2026-4417, a remotely triggerable crash in TLS 1.3 handshake parsing. Install today.",
          "reasoning": "The advisory is rated important and the affected code path (TLS 1.3 server-side handshake) is reachable by anything on this box that terminates TLS: sshd is unaffected, but a local web server such as Caddy is. There is no configuration workaround. The fix is a point release on the same 3.5 branch with no API changes, so applying it is low risk and needs no reboot; long-running services pick it up on restart.",
          "notes_excerpt": "openssl 3.5.2 \u2014 security release\n\n* CVE-2026-4417: out-of-bounds read while parsing a malformed ClientHello\n  with a truncated key_share extension. A remote peer can crash any\n  process accepting TLS 1.3 connections. Severity: important.\n* Fixed a memory leak in X509_STORE_CTX when verification fails early.",
          "notes_url": "https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/FEDORA-2026-8d31e5",
